From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:49:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: expose native rendering accessors and FontFace state

Expose FontFace.status, Screen.colorDepth/pixelDepth, and the two
constant TextMetrics bounds/baseline values as getter-only native Web IDL
accessors with enumerable/configurable descriptors and receiver checks.
Keep the existing synthetic screen depths and text metric values.

Start local/URL FontFace instances unloaded. Reading loaded creates one
pending promise without initiating loading; load enters loading and queues
synthetic successful completion with loaded status before resolution.
Keep the resolver GC-traced in private wrapper state and root the face only
while its task is scheduled. Preserve load/loaded promise identity, original
FontFace fulfillment, reentrancy, and scheduler cancellation cleanup.
Update the existing upstream initial-status assertion; add no tests.

This remains a synthetic successful font model, not font fetching, parsing,
rasterization, or full FontFaceSet integration. The benchmark is unchanged.

References:
https://drafts.csswg.org/css-font-loading/#fontface-interface
https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#the-screen-interface
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#textmetrics

Validation: all 1658 existing upstream tests and 76 temporary API checks
pass. Benchmark improves from 111/130 to 112/130 (86.15%) with only
rendering-property-descriptors changing; font-load-semantics still passes.
One reviewer pass found no actionable issues.
